# noninteractive  (generated by harness/noninteractive.sh)
# A hook must be completely silent outside an interactive shell.

bash -c  (sources adapter)                     fd3_bytes=0    verdict=SILENT_as_required
bash script.sh                                 fd3_bytes=0    verdict=SILENT_as_required
bash -i -c  (interactive forced)               fd3_bytes=0    verdict=SILENT_as_required
zsh -f -c (sources adapter)                    fd3_bytes=0    verdict=SILENT_as_required
zsh -f script                                  fd3_bytes=0    verdict=SILENT_as_required
zsh -f -i -c (interactive forced)              fd3_bytes=0    verdict=SILENT_as_required
fish -c (sources adapter)                      fd3_bytes=0    verdict=SILENT_as_required
fish script.fish                               fd3_bytes=0    verdict=SILENT_as_required

EXPECTED: every line above reads SILENT_as_required.
fd3_bytes is the number of bytes the adapter wrote to its sink FD.
Note: the adapters install their hooks only when the shell reports
itself interactive, so the non-interactive paths return before
installing anything.
